                        </STLBBauID>
                      </STLBBau>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <ComplTSA>Yes</ComplTSA>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Layer of geotextiles, nonwoven, for separation, acc. to FGSV leaflet on the use of geosynthetics in earthworks of road construction (M Geok E), geotextile robustness class 4, mass min. 250 g/m2, static puncture force min. 2,5 kN, on soil group SU (sand-[PERSON_033]-mixture), installation in road, overlap width min. 20 cm, billing by the developed area of the worked surfaces, execution acc. to individual description,</span>
                            <br/>
                          </Text>
                          <TextComplement Kind="Owner" MarkLbl="11" ArtChrIdent="-484">
                            <ComplCaption>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Individual description no. </span>
                            </ComplCaption>
                            <ComplBody>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">'Execution for filter-stable separation of installed [PERSON_112] from in-situ soils, after prior consultation with the site management. .Execution applies to all soil groups of the prevaling geology...................................................'</span>
                            </ComplBody>
                            <ComplTail>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </ComplTail>
                          </TextComplement>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Geotextile nonwoven separation robustn.-cl.4 overlap-B 20cm</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007903" RNoPart="0004">
                    <Qty>15.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Exposing lines of all kinds, down to the subgrade of the road as </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">difficulty surcharge </span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">to the item loosen soil for road surfaces.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">If several lines lie together up to a spacing of 1,00 m, the length of the lines is measured only 1 time.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Supply and re-covering with sand is to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: line crossings/ exposures in the course of the civil works are paid               in the trade civil works water pipeline!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Exposing lines of all kinds, down to the subgrade of the road as </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2007905" RNoPart="03">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Demolition works / reinstatement area [PROJEKT_001]</span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007912" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>30.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Cut asphalt pavement, thickness of the pavement over 8 to 16 cm, execution with joint cutter, depth up to 120 mm, separate remaining thickness.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Cut asphalt pavement D 5-10cm T 100mm</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007914" RNoPart="0002">
                    <Qty>50.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Break up and take up bituminous pavement,       </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">in areas alongside carriageways, footpaths and cycle paths,              </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">thickness of the bituminous pavement </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">8 to 16 cm,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">send demolition asphalt to recycling see following note.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: The reclaimed asphalt according to analysis with PAH - values =&lt; 25 mg/kg </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">is to be classified acc. to RuVA - StB 01 (table 1) as not containing tar, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">but corresponds acc. to LAGA and UVM of 13.04.2004 </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">to the assignment value </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Z 1.1.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">All associated costs of disposal/reprocessing are to be included in the price as well.   </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Arising materials become the property of the AN and are to be disposed of at the expense of the AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Reinstallation within the overall project is not permitted!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution in asphalted inter-municipal connecting roads and field paths,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">as well as areas alongside roads. </span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Break up and take up bituminous pavement,       </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2007923" RNoPart="04">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Roads, paths, squares </span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2007924">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">The installation of soil replacement materials to be supplied is planned as follows:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The pipe surround/ trench backfilling as well as the road and path construction are executed as follows: </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Substrate improvement only if needed with [PERSON_182] 0/X after prior</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">  consultation with the site management of the AG !</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Lower bedding layer main water pipeline DN 300 ZMU d = 10 cm gravel 0/16.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Side and top cover ZMU pipe DN 300 with in-situ re-        usable soil material of HB A and B.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Remaining trench backfilling above cover up to UK frost protection layer 0/45 road,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">  or UK crushed stone 0/45 path sub-base, likewise with  in-situ re-              usable soil material HB A and B.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Exception remaining trench backfilling with [PERSON_182] 0/X to be supplied in areas    with in-situ soil material that cannot be reinstalled, but only after         prior consultation with the site management of the AG !</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_182] 0/45 only in the area of paved surfaces </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">  asphalt, in unpaved areas such as forest paths crushed stone 0/45. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Trench width at excavation bottom acc. to EN 1610  GGG pipe DN 300 ZMU</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">B = 1,20 m vertical with shoring</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Trench width acc. to EN 1610 sloped 45° to 60°,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">trench width at bottom (OK bedding layer = UK pipe)</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for 1 x GGG DN 300 ZMU or 1 x PE DA 355,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">B = 0,75 m without shoring</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, (B = excavation bottom of 0,55 m/45° - 0,65 m/60°).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Dimensions rounded.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note for all materials to be supplied with installation in the area of </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">existing groundwater:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The entire additional expenditure for compliance with all regulations regarding safety and hygiene for the protection of the groundwater is to be included in the corresponding items material supply.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">All materials, components and construction aids used in the new construction project must not adversely affect the [PERSON_029] either hygienically or chemically. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">This applies in particular to materials, components and auxiliary construction materials that go not into the structure, but into the water pipeline trench.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The installation of soil replacement materials to be supplied is planned as follows:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007925" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>35.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Supply and install a </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">combined frost protection, gravel base course,</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">in carriageways, agricultural roads, footpaths and cycle paths and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">ancillary areas with bound surface course (asphalt surfacing).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Degree of compaction DPr min. 103 % of gravel-sand mixture grading 0/32 mm and 0/45 mm</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">billing acc. to fill profiles and proof by weighbridge tickets,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">total layer thickness up to approx. 50 cm thick.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: Should [PERSON_182] 0/X be installed as substrate improvement below the frost protection, gravel base course in the path area                        , </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">               this material is billed as well in the trade civil works water pipeline in the course of the                 remaining trench backfilling.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Supply and install a combined frost protection, gravel base course, </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007929" RNoPart="0002">
                    <Qty>240.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">but supply, install and compact a crushed-stone base course of</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">moraine - crushed stone, grading up to 0/45.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Installed thickness up to 60 cm, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">execution as forest path sub-base up to approx. 10 cm below OK forest path, ground,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">incl. pre-profiling of the surface in crowned profile to receive the surface course d = approx. 10 cm. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Path width on average approx. 3,00 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note: The top layer d = 10 cm is produced later by a company of the                     forest owners, a review in advance takes place </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">                jointly with the AN of the water pipeline project.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007926" RNoPart="0003">
                    <Qty>25.000</Qty>
                    <QU>t</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">but supply, install and compact a crushed-stone base course of</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">moraine - crushed stone grading 0/22 - 0/44.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Installed thickness up to 10 cm.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution as top crushed-stone base course in forest and connecting paths after completion</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of all civil works water pipeline GGG DN 300 and PE DA 355.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing with weighbridge tickets by</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">tonnes!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">It must be possible to assign the weighbridge tickets unambiguously to the item tendered here </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Ongoing coordination with the site management of the AG has to take place!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: execution and billing only in access and exit routes in the nearer                area of the civil works, after express consultation with the                site management of the AG!             </span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007927" RNoPart="0004">
                    <Qty>15.000</Qty>
                    <QU>t</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">but supply and install a hydraulically bound surface course of</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">moraine - crushed stone grading 0/11 - 0/16.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Installed thickness approx. 2 - 4  cm.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution as top surface course in forest and connecting paths </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">after completion of all civil works water pipeline GGG DN 300 and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">PE DA 355.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing with weighbridge tickets by tonnes!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">It must be possible to assign the weighbridge tickets unambiguously to the item tendered here </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Coordination before execution with the site management of the AG has to take place without fail!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: execution and billing only in access and exit routes in the nearer                area of the civil works, after express consultation with the                site management of the AG!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007930" RNoPart="0005">
                    <Qty>60.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the item gravel and crushed-stone base course for fine grading incl.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">compaction in the area of roads, agricultural roads, footpaths and cycle paths and side areas EV 2 =&gt; 120 MN/m²  =  EVD =&gt; 65 MN/m², </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">(ZTV- SoB) on OK KTS/ STS,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">to receive all </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">asphalt surfacings</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The pricing of the fine grading is accordingly omitted in the items gravel and crushed-stone base course.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note: Billing is done exclusively only for the fine grading                     under asphalt areas, the fine grading of the </span>
                            </p>
