                  <Remark ID="GW_2007975">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note on the items strip and re-spread topsoil,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">based on the present soil protection concept:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Where topsoil is stored temporarily in heaps, in advance of the</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">topsoil stripping above-ground plant parts are to be removed as far as possible,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">in order to be able to minimise harmful decomposition during temporary storage in heaps</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">During temporary storage the biological activity of the topsoil is to be preserved.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Necessary therefore are sufficient aeration, protection against waterlogging and resupply of organic matter by greening.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Minimisation of driving on areas and maximum reduction of transport distances, use of tracked excavators with long-stick buckets; </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">no use of bulldozers and wheeled vehicles.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">No driving on the surrounding open areas (e.g. agricultural areas);</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">unavoidable driving over only with vehicles of low ground pressure (tracked vehicles or tractors with tipping trailer, wheeled vehicles only in combination with suitable underlays).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">This applies to cut and fill areas!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">The estimator is urgently recommended to inspect the corresponding,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">available soil protection concept!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p/>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007976" RNoPart="0008">
                    <Qty>6200.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Topsoil of humus soil, [PERSON_033],   </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">dark brown, soft, moist slightly clayey-fine sandy,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">slightly humic,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">strip, </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">stripping thickness</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> between 30 and 50 cm = </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">on average 40 cm.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Store material at the side on proper, trapezoidal, loosely tipped stockpiles</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">with a height of max. 1,50 - 2,00 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The surfaces of the stockpiles are to be lightly smoothed for better drainage.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The topsoil stockpiles must not be used as storage area </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">or driven on! </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">After completion of the pipeline and civil works</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">pick up topsoil again and spread it on the</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">original areas.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Spreading thickness</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> between 30 and 50 cm = </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">on average 40 cm.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing by area measurement.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note on the topsoil thicknesses determined as follows:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 1/25  d = 0,50 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 2/25  d = 0,40 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 3/25  d = 0,30 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 4/25  d = 0,40 m. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Excavation and re-spreading on average approx. 0,40 m.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Topsoil of humus soil, [PERSON_033],   </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007978" RNoPart="0009">
                    <Qty>100.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the item strip topsoil 30 to 50  cm = on average 40 cm thick, store at the side and re-spread,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for additional hauling of topsoil, incl. required </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">intermediate storage at the [PERSON_125] of the AN within the project.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution exclusively only after prior consultation with the site management of the AG, in areas lacking storage possibilities at the side directly next to topsoil stripping and as compensation for different spreading thicknesses.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing by haulage reports in direct agreement with the AG,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">determination of quantities in compacted state!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the item strip topsoil 30 to 50  cm = on average 40 cm thick, store at the side and re-spread,</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007979" RNoPart="0010">
                    <Qty>9300.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pure surcharge to the item strip and re-spread topsoil for:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Produce fine grading for agriculturally used planting and meadow areas before the respective seeding works, loosen thoroughly, mill and produce the required evenness, permissible deviation from the target level 3 cm; gap under the 4-m straightedge up to 5 cm, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">picking off of stones and foreign bodies from 3 cm Ø, as well as of weeds and plant parts that rot with difficulty, these materials are to be transported to an approved landfill, disposal site or recycling plant at the [PERSON_125] of the contractor.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Before execution a consultation, coordination with the respective plot owner and/or tenant has to take place.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">It is left to the AN to have this work executed directly by the respective plot owner and/or tenant.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is via the item tendered here by area actually worked in m2!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pure surcharge to the item strip and re-spread topsoil for:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2031515">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note on meadow seeding:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">After completion of the works (topsoil spreading in meadow plots) the municipality plans to discuss the seeding of the meadow areas directly with the respective owners, or tenants and have it executed.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The item seeding is therefore tendered as contingency item.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The item produce fine grading for meadow seeding (preparatory works), </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">is tendered as normal item, but the AG reserves the right</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">to have this work too, under certain circumstances, executed directly by the respective owners/tenants </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note on meadow seeding:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007984" RNoPart="0011">
                    <Qty>6200.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pure surcharge to the item strip and re-spread topsoil for:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Loosen thoroughly substrate (cultivated soil) for agriculturally used meadow areas before the re-spreading of topsoil ( cultivator tilling ).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Before execution a consultation, coordination with the respective plot owner and/or tenant has to take place.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">It is left to the AN to have this work executed directly by the respective plot owner and/or tenant.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is via the item tendered here by area actually worked in m2!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pure surcharge to the item strip and re-spread topsoil for:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007985" RNoPart="0012">
                    <Qty>200.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Humus soil, soil group 1 DIN 18915, supply and spread, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">spreading area inclined, spreading thickness on average [TELEFON_036] cm.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution as supplement to the existing humus soil.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing by delivery notes.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Humus soil, soil group 1 DIN 18915, supply and spread, </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2007986">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note on the items open trench excavation water pipelines:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">In the excavation items all homogeneous zones occurring according to the geotechnical report are described with the respective percentage shares of the total excavation.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The soil classes acc. to old DIN 18300 range from</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">soil class 3 to 4.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Only occasionally, in various homogeneous zones,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">with possible occurrence of boulders, soil class 6 can occur.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The additional expenditure of this soil class is paid in a separate </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">surcharge item.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">All other soil classes 3 to 4  and where occurring also 5 are to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Pipe bedding, pipe surround and pipe cover as follows:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For the main line GGG DN 300 ZMU only a bedding layer D = 10 cm with [PERSON_182] 0/16 to be supplied is executed as pipe bedding, the side backfilling and upper cover is made with in-situ [PERSON_093] up to max. 100 mm stone size.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Where PE DA 355 pipes are laid in open-cut construction, these are </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">likewise laid on 10 cm bedding layer 0/16, the pipe surround and pipe cover up to 30 cm above pipe crown, are additionally to be executed with </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">[PERSON_182] 0/16 to be supplied.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The [PERSON_182] 0/16 (8/16 with wet substrate) is paid separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p/>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2019755">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note on all [ORT_030]:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The civil works are essentially tendered acc. to the new DIN 18300 (2015-08)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">[ORT_030] on the basis of DIN 4020 geotechnical investigations for construction purposes with the corresponding homogeneous zones </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The basis is the geotechnical report by fm - Geotechnik</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">engineering office for geotechnics.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The homogeneous zones listed here are described in detail in the relevant </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">excavation items with their respective, estimated proportional quantities</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB A1: fills gravel</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">           soil class DIN 18300 (2012-09)   3, 4, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB A2: fill [PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">           soil class DIN 18300 (2012-09)   4</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB B 1: peat</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">           soil class DIN 18300 (2012-09)   2/4</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB B 2:  weathered loam/slightly weathered ground moraine</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">           soil class DIN 18300 (2012-09)   4</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB B 3:  moraine sand</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">           soil class DIN 18300 (2012-09)   2,3,4</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB B 4:  moraine gravel</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">           soil class DIN 18300 (2012-09)   3,4</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB B 5:  ground moraine, [PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">           soil class DIN 18300 (2012-09)   4</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">As the cohesive soils encountered are partly sensitive to water, these soils can soften with improper temporary storage and with heavy precipitation during a transport or through mechanical stress, so that they may pass into soil class 2 acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09) or into a pulpy consistency.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">The AN</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">has to ensure</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">that these sensitive soils do not</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">pass into soil class 2.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">A payment for soil class 2 does not take place!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note on all [ORT_030]:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2019748">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Overview of all homogeneous zones in the area of open-cut construction.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Open-cut construction water pipeline trenches sloped and shored:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 1</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, with 3 soil groups, soil group 1 GU DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 2 GU* DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 3 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 1 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 4 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone A 1 fill,gravel soil class 3,4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 50 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 2000 to 2200 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content up to 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- relative density medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 5 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 4</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, with 2 soil groups, soil group 1 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), soil group 2 UM DIN 18196 (medium plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 3 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 65 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 2 weathered loam/weathered ground moraine soil class 4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 55 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 75 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 10 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 1800 to 2000 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained from 20 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained to 60 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content over 10 to 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic from 0,5,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic to 0,75,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip from 4 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip to 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 3 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 5,</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> with 3 soil groups, soil group 1 SW DIN 18196 (well-graded sand-gravel mixture), soil group 2 SU DIN 18196 (sand-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 3 SU* DIN 18196 (sand-[PERSON_033] mixture), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 4 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 11 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 3 moraine sand soil class 2,3,4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 1 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 3 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 30 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 1800 to 2000 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained from 0,15 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained to 0,5 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content over 20 to 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- relative density loose to medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 up to 3 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 6</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, with 2 soil groups, soil group 1 GU DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 2 GU* DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 1 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 4 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 4 moraine gravel soil class 3,4,(6)depending on share of the size of the cobbles and boulders/with firm consistency soil class 6 possible) acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 30 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 50 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 1 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 10 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction boulders DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Bo) upper value 4,9 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction large boulders DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (LBo) upper value 4,9 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 2000 to 2200 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained from 0,45 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained to 0,65 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content over 10 to 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- relative density medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 up to 3 %.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Overview of all homogeneous zones in the area of open-cut construction.</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007987" RNoPart="0013">
                    <Qty>95.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Trench excavation new construction [PROJEKT_001]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Soil of the trenches</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for water pipelines for </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">GGG ZMU DN 300</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">(and short lengths </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">PE DA 355</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> at the transitions where the material changes)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">shafts and structures,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">excavate true to profile </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">in shoring</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">after</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">removal</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of a surface pavement (path crossing asphalt)), </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">or after topsoil stripping (meadow plots),</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">or from OK forest tracks with gravel/crushed stone.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Shoring is to be included in the price as well!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Backfill and compact in roads and paths acc. to the Additional Technical Contract Conditions and Guidelines for Excavations in Traffic Areas (ZTVA-StB). </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Backfill and compact in agriculturally used meadow and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">arable areas with gentle construction method, based on the present </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">soil protection concept. (see separate item)  </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Excessive compaction of the cultivated soil is to be avoided! </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Displaced soil from pipe and pipe support, [PERSON_112] to be supplied for poss. subsoil improvemment, remaining trench backfilling and combined</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">frost protection/ gravel base course is hauled away.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The hauling away and removal is paid separately in the following surcharge - items depending on </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">contamination. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The supply of the [PERSON_112] is paid separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The installation of all gravel materials in the trench is to be included in the price here.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Excavation depth depending on surface removal 1,60 m to 2,00 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">corresponds to a pipe cover (OK pipe crown to OK ground)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of approx. 1,50 m to approx. 1,85 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Greater excavation depths for possibly requred subsoil improvements below the 10 cm thick bedding layer, are paid separately in a surcharge item.                               </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Base width of the trenches in m (acc. to DIN EN 1610).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Trench width acc. to EN 1610  GGG pipe DN 300  b = 1,20 m with shoring</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note: Due to the local conditions (partly ground-</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">               water extraction, water-sensitive soils or confined con                  ditions in the forest area), </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">               the length of the open, shored water pipeline trench is, in </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">	dependence on the pipe lengths of 6 m, to be kept as short as possible (up to 8 m)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">	!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">: In the area of the water pipeline shaft the </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">               additional excavation with re-backfilling, compared with the </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">               main water pipeline trench, is charged as surcharge item excavation, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">               just as the shoring in the shaft area itself, paid separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing shored in areas that are laid out as traffic routes, forest tracks or access roads and areas with possibly required groundwater lowering: </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Station approx. 0+570 - 0+580, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Station approx. 0+740 - 0+750,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Station approx. 0+985 - 0+995,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Station approx. 0+995 - 1+067,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Before execution of the overall project the areas trench excavation</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">shored or sloped are discussed once more on site with the executing civil works company and the site management of the AG.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The areas listed are essentially to be adhered to in this way!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">The estimator has to observe the following homogeneous zones acc. to DIN 18300 </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">with their percentage shares of the total excavation:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 1</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, with 3 soil groups, soil group 1 GU DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 2 GU* DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 3 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 1 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 4 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone A 1 fill,gravel soil class 3,4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 50 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 2000 to 2200 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content up to 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- relative density medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 5 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 4</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, with 2 soil groups, soil group 1 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), soil group 2 UM DIN 18196 (medium plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 3 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 65 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 2 weathered loam/weathered ground moraine soil class 4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 55 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 75 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 10 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 1800 to 2000 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained from 20 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained to 60 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content over 10 to 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic from 0,5,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic to 0,75,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip from 4 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip to 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 3 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 5,</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> with 3 soil groups, soil group 1 SW DIN 18196 (well-graded sand-gravel mixture), soil group 2 SU DIN 18196 (sand-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 3 SU* DIN 18196 (sand-[PERSON_033] mixture), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 4 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 11 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 3 moraine sand soil class 2,3,4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 1 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 3 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 30 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 1800 to 2000 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained from 0,15 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained to 0,5 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content over 20 to 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- relative density loose to medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 up to 3 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 6</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, with 2 soil groups, soil group 1 GU DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 2 GU* DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 1 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 4 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 4 moraine gravel soil class 3,4,(6)depending on share of the size of the cobbles and boulders/with firm consistency soil class 6 possible) acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 30 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 50 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 1 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 10 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction boulders DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Bo) upper value 4,9 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction large boulders DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (LBo) upper value 4,9 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- moist density soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 2000 to 2200 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained from 0,45 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- shear strength undrained to 0,65 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content over 10 to 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- relative density medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 up to 3 %.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Billing of the water pipeline trench in lfm!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Trench excavation new construction [PROJEKT_001]</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2007988" RNoPart="0014">
                    <Qty>580.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">but </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">trench excavation sloped 45°</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> depending on the in-situ</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">[PERSON_093] (see geotechnical report) </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">without shoring</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for water pipeline pipes 1 x GGG DN 300 ZMU or 1 x PE DA 355,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">with single laying.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Trench width acc. to EN 1610 sloped 45°,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">trench width at bottom (OK bedding layer = UK pipe)</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">  </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">B = 0,76 m without shoring</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, (B = excavation base 0,56 m/45°).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Dimensions rounded.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing in areas (predominantly meadow plots) that are not laid out as traffic routes or access roads.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">According to the geotechnical report this concerns predominantly the following areas:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Area existing water pipeline DN 300 start of construction - station approx. 0+000</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Station approx. 0+000 - 0+570 (transition shored trench and directional drillings)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Meadows as agricultural areas in the area of the ram core soundings 1 to 4 with the following geological descriptions(soil/[PERSON_093]):</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 1 humus soil, [PERSON_033]       OK -  0,50 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">         moraine sand                    0,50 - 1,40 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">         moraine gravel                      1,40- 3,20 m</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">         ground moraine                     3,20 - 6,00 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 2 humus soil, [PERSON_033]                OK - 0,40 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">           weathered loam, [PERSON_033]     0,40 - 1,30 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">            ground moraine weathered      1,30 - 2,60 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">            ground moraine                         2,60 - 4,00 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 3 humus soil, [PERSON_033]               OK - 0,30 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">           weathered loam, [PERSON_033]    0,30 - 1,20 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">           moraine gravel                           1,20 - 2,60 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">           moraine sand                          2,60 - 4,00 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 4 humus soil, [PERSON_033]               OK -  0,40 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">           weathered loam, [PERSON_033]      0,40 - 1,90 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">           moraine gravel                             1,90 - 2,80 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">           ground moraine                           2,80 - 4,00 m. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Before execution of the overall project the areas trench excavation</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">shored or sloped are discussed once more on site with the executing civil works company and the site management of the AG.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The areas listed are essentially to be adhered to in this way!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note on the slope and max. length of open trench acc. to report:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Due to the local conditions (partly ground-</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">water extraction and water-sensitive soils</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">the length of the open, sloped water pipeline trench is, in </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">dependence on the pipe lengths of 6 m, to be kept as short as possible (up to 8 m)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Should the AN execute a longer open trench in dry weather,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">this is in any case to be backfilled again up to UK topsoil on the same day.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">The exposed slopes are, just like sensitive soils (excavation), to be protected with tarpaulins or similar at the [PERSON_125] of the AN against </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">weather influences, this work is likewise to be included in the price here in </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">the trench excavation item!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Work as item last described in full wording,</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
