              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2008089" RNoPart="05">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Shaft structures concrete works and civil works [PROJEKT_001]</span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2008090">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note for the execution/placing of the following items water pipeline shafts:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The [PERSON_006] angular clear dimension 2,00 x 3,00 m, station 0+000 can, owing to its dead weight, only be placed by means of a heavy-duty crane </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">This work is to be included in the price of the item supply and place shaft and is not paid separately!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">A corresponding site road from the asphalt path to station 0+000 is paid separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The two round water pipeline shafts DN 2500 can be transported and placed on site with</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">suitable crawler excavators ([TELEFON_036] to).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Shaft DN 2500 at station 0+370 can be transported from the asphalt path via the water pipeline route to the installation location.(</span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">approx. 270 m</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Shaft DN 2500 at approx. station 1+000 (forest area) is accessible via a gravel path from [ADRESSE_018].</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">B 12 to start of forest approx. 260 m, start of forest to installation location approx. 320 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Total from B 12 </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">approx. 580</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> m gravel path.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Should the AN decide to lift in precast elements DN 2500 with e.g. 2 excavators, the 2 excavator is to be in cluded in the price of the complete construction of the </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">shaft structure.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Additional payment beyond the item construct shaft structure complete, is not made!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">The estimator has to observe this!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note for the execution/placing of the following items water pipeline shafts:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008110" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Safety ladder acc. to DIN EN 14396,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DVGW 351, BGV D 36</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">entirely of [PERSON_115] material no. 1.4301/1.4307</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">rungs of U-profile with perforated tread surface, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">30 mm, slip resistance R 13, step height 280 mm,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">clear ladder width 400 mm.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Stiles of special profile of high stiffness (57x25x2,5 mm),</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">covered at the top with PVC - caps.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Incl. height-adjustable wall brackets for anchor fixing,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">which ensure a minimum tread depth of 150 mm (distance [PERSON_074] to</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">centre of rung).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Incl. all fixing materials of [PERSON_115], assemble with</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">through-bolt anchors HST - R M10 in shaft wall.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Shaft depth </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">T = 2,35</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> m from OK entry to shaft floor,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">with access aid, plug-on, EH S, executed as ladder</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">extension, entirely of [PERSON_115],</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">height approx. 1200 mm,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Make: e.g. [FIRMA_062]-[PERSON_115], [PERSON_129] SIS1</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">               [PERSON_129] A) vertical installation</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">or equivalent make,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Make / [PERSON_129]: ____________________</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: execution in the angular precast shaft at start of construction 0+000.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Safety ladder acc. to DIN EN 14396,</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
