                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> to item trench excavation water pipeline main line </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for all additional efforts in the area of [PERSON_006],</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">excavation sloped, excavation depth up to approx. 3,0 m incl. subsoil improvement,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">and outlet shaft drainage DA 110,  </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">backfilling with in-situ material, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">hauling away and removal of the soil displacement of </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">[PERSON_006] </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">2,00 x 3,00 m</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> in clear dimension.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Locate existing water pipeline GGG DN 300, expose all round for the pipe tie-in, secure incl. all required manual and locating work.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Attention: line must not be damaged before the pipe tie-in!</span>
