                  <Item ID="GW_2008518" RNoPart="0024">
                    <Qty>675.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to all pipe-laying items</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for the dimensionally accurate pipe laying for the cast iron pipe and PE - line DN 300/DA355, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">(accurate in position and level +/- 1cm) according to documents or taking into account the enclosed site plans and the longitudinal sections because of the low gradient of the planned partial sections of the cast iron pipeline. Compliance with the design for level and position of the pipeline is mandatory in order to avoid intermediate high points and thus air inclusions or to ensure the performance of the pipeline.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The dimensionally accurate construction of the pipe trench is to be checked and documented by a continuously performed digital target/actual position and level measurement or survey with Gauß-Krüger coordinates on the pipe invert.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Deviations of the dimensionally accurate pipe laying (above the tolerance of 1cm) are to be remedied by the AN immediately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction of the pipe trench in sections and thus all auxiliary and ancillary costs necessary for it as well as the increased time and effort are to be included in the EP.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to all pipe-laying items for the dimensionally accurate pipe laying for the cast iron pipe and PE - line DN 300/DA355, </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008519" RNoPart="0025">
                    <Qty>675.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pressure pipe of ductile cast iron, cement-lined inside </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DN 300 PN 16, for drinking water, clean. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge for the cleaning of the pressure pipeline DN 300</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">/</span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">DA 355</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> before commissioning during pipe laying with a sponge rubber ball or with a cleaning pig or a pipe brush incl. pulling rope or pulling rods, suitable for drinking water, at the contractor's (AN) [PERSON_125] (but in consultation with the AG) during execution also in partial sections (of the pipe-laying works) as continuous cleaning for the pipe's internal protection. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">(Note: For effective cleaning the insert must be approx. 8-12 % larger than the pipe inside diameter DN 300.)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The costs for the supply, execution in sections, incl. all difficulties, obstructions as well as documentation are to be included in the EP. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Inserting, pulling and recovering the pig or the cleaning brush has to take place in sections in each case at the pipe ends and flange ends of the pipeline </span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DN 300. Included are the required working times as well as the provision of all required</span>
                              <span style="font-size:11pt;background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">equipment, incl. ancillary work.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pressure pipe of ductile cast iron, cement-lined inside </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008520" RNoPart="0026">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge for setting a respective pipe stopper bladder DN 300 and an end cap with seal, for [PERSON_076], suitable for drinking water, for pipe laying, as additional safety barrier during the construction phase and for protection against ingress of extraneous water and wastewater.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Setting and removing the pipe stopper bladder and the end cap is to be done in each case after completion of the daily laying works or before the start of the works. The repeated setting up, as well as repeated filling etc. are to be provided for the entire construction measure, also with laying in sections incl. ancillary work.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">With pipe laying in sections several pipe stopper bladders and end caps are to be kept available on site.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge for setting a respective pipe stopper bladder DN 300 and an end cap with seal, for [PERSON_076], suitable for drinking water, for pipe laying, as additional safety barrier during the construction phase and for protection against ingress of extraneous water and wastewater.</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2008551">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Supply and installation of parts not individually            </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">listed here of the main line and of the house connections are paid in the price lists at the list price Raab - Karcher, [FIRMA_067], [FIRMA_010] and other suppliers with discount or mark-up. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">In the following items discount or mark-up are to be stated in %;                          </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The settlement price is to be shown.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Supply and installation of parts not individually            </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
