            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2008279" RNoPart="05">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Emergency supplies house connections </span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2008280">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note for the following items emergency supplies house connections</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">These works are essentially for removal, - and reinstallation</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of emergency supplies of existing water line house connections,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">in the course of the overall measure water line laying. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Smooth coordination with the civil works crew is</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">absolutely necessary.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Disagreements are to be settled internally and must not be at the expense</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of the AG.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Before execution of the works, the responsible</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">water master Mr [PERSON_104] is to be informed in every case and the sequence </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">coordinated with him!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p/>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008281" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Set up emergency lines (emergency supply) with PE - pipes DN 32 - 40, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">maintain, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">secure and remove again after completion of the measure. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The joints and connections are to be priced with complete connection material (fittings, branches etc.).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution for the water line house connection [PERSON_062]. 19.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">For hygienic reasons new lines are to be used.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Shutting off the existing house connection line and coordination with the resident incl. timely notification of those affected </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">is to be included in the price here.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;margin-left:1pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">It is to be ensured that the connected customers are constantly supplied with [PERSON_029].</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Emergency lines are to be constructed for 1 building.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Connection to the existing [PERSON_006] DZ NZ Isnyberg 401.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Connection length for the house up to approx. 150 m </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is 1 x lump sum.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Necessary covering works are carried out by the civil works company (crossings, access drives etc.). </span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Set up emergency lines (emergency supply) with PE - pipes DN 32 - 40, </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008282" RNoPart="0002">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">After dismantling of the emergency supplies/bypass lines and recommissioning</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of the local water supply line,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">remove, clean and reinstall the strainer insert on the                       </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">house connection lines of the respective houses.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution as required.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">After dismantling of the emergency supplies/bypass lines and recommissioning</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2008575" RNoPart="06">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Leak test and disinfection</span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008576" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>425.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <STLBBau>
                        <STLBBauCtlg>
                          <CtlgName>STLB-Bau</CtlgName>
                          <VersDate>2025-04</VersDate>
                          <WCtg>043</WCtg>
                          <Group>1057</Group>
                        </STLBBauCtlg>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>-484</ArtChrIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>2136</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>2</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>2770</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>112</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>5603</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>121</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>5606</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>3</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>6611</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>31</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>6645</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>4</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>9945</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>46</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>10164</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>3</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                      </STLBBau>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <ComplTSA>Yes</ComplTSA>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Flush pressure pipeline before commissioning, disinfect DVGW W 291, for drinking water, made of PE, with [PERSON_029], sterilising agent hydrogen peroxide, incl. disinfectant, DN 355, execution according to individual description,</span>
                            <br/>
                          </Text>
                          <TextComplement Kind="Owner" MarkLbl="11" ArtChrIdent="-484">
                            <ComplCaption>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Individual description no. </span>
                            </ComplCaption>
                            <ComplBody>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">'Execution in the area of the 2 direcctional bores with the respective transitions to the GGG DN 300 ZMU pipes).'</span>
                            </ComplBody>
                            <ComplTail>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </ComplTail>
                          </TextComplement>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Flush disinfect pressure pipe DW [PERSON_029] hydrogen peroxide disinfectant DN355</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008577" RNoPart="0002">
                    <Qty>655.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pressure pipe made of ductile cast iron, cement-lined inside </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DN 300 PN 16, for drinking water, disinfect</span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pressure pipeline DN 300 before commissioning to be filled in a dosed manner with [PERSON_029] and with hydrogen peroxide – disinfectant, according to DVGW  W 291 (however in agreement with the AG, in sections (approx. 2-3 sections),</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">or after coordination with the local site management and the AG). </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The disinfection solution has to remain in the pipeline for a time of 24 hours. Included are the necessary working times as well as the provision of all necessary equipment, fittings, valves and standpipes for the pipeline, cement-lined inside, DN 300. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The necessary drinking water is provided by the AG and is to be disposed of by the AN. Proof of successful disinfection is to be furnished and communicated in writing.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pressure pipe of ductile cast iron, cement-lined inside </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008578" RNoPart="0003">
                    <Qty>655.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pressure pipe made of ductile cast iron, cement-lined inside </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DN 300 PN 16, for drinking water, flush</span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">. </span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                                   </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Flush line DN 300 GGG - only with drinking water, flush temporary supply lines before use, flushing velocity in the line at least 0,6 m/s, flushing quantity 3 to 6 times the pipe content. Water meters must not be flushed through. Water withdrawal from installations in operation only in agreement with the AG. The flushing water must not get into parts of the water supply installations that are in operation. The flushing water from the flushed line is to be discharged without causing damage.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For the flushing the [PERSON_029] is made available by the AG free of charge. Bringing in the [PERSON_029] for the flushing is to be carried out in coordination with the local construction supervision and the AG.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Flush pressure pipeline before commissioning, for drinking water, DN 300, in sections or after coordination with the local site management and the AG, incl. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The supply, the installation and removal of all fittings and valves necessary for flushing is to be included in the price. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">All safety-relevant works have to be carried out from the point of view of the hazard analysis according to DVGW guidelines.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The flushing of [ORT_031] for drinking water is carried out according to DIN 2000, DIN 19360 and the DVGW - worksheet  W 291.  The flushing water is provided by the AG and is to be disposed of by the AN. Professional flushing according to W 291 or W 346 for the removal of unintentionally introduced foreign matter and auxiliary materials.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The carrying out of the flushing is to be notified in writing 1 week before it is carried out and coordinated with the local construction supervision and the AG. The flushing is to be documented and the proof is to be communicated to the AG in writing.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution in approx. 2 - 3  sections.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pressure pipe of ductile cast iron, cement-lined inside </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2008585">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: pressure tests PE - pipes DN/OD 355 and GGG DN 300 ZMU</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The following items pressure tests are tendered according to DIN EN 805.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Following this DIN EN 805, the specifications from the DVGW</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">W 400 - 2 (2022) also apply.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Before execution of a pressure test, the permissible test pressure as well as the type of execution depending on the pipe material, taking into account the respective depth, is determined jointly by the AG and AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Depending on the construction sequence, partial sections can be carried out separately, or together as an overall pressure test.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The respective max. permissible test pressure for cast iron and PE - pipes must not be exceeded. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p/>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
