                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the items pressure test for:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the cast iron pipe laying and main pressure test DN 300</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for carrying out a continuous pressure test for improved safety and risk minimisation of leakages, by means of an oil-, [PERSON_029]-, and pollen-free compressed air compressor's, approved for drinking water, for checking every pipe joint in the pipe string during the construction of the cast iron pipeline DN 300 </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">incl. all equipment, machines, increased personnel deployment and accessories and consideration of the increased time required for all occupational safety guidelines incl. waiting times for carrying out the continuous pressure test (in agreement with the local construction supervision and the AG) according to DVGW guideline G 469 with maximum 1,5bar pressure.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Possible leakages found are to be located and immediately to at the cost of the AN to be remedied.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">All safety-relevant works have to be carried out from the point of view of the hazard analysis according to DVGW guidelines.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Total length approx. 655 m in 2 spatially separate areas.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the items pressure test for:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2008590">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note on the drinking water analysis:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">In addition to the drinking water analyses on the water line to be newly</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">laid (in several partial sections like pressure tests),  the following works are carried out:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Before the start of the water line works, in agreement with the responsible</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">water master Mr [PERSON_104], a drinking water sample is taken from the existing water line network for comparison and evaluated.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note on the drinking water analysis:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008290" RNoPart="0007">
                    <Qty>5.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Microbiological drinking water analysis according to the Drinking Water Ordinance V, annex 1,2,5 </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">(E-Coli, [PERSON_160], Aeromonas, colony count,  </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">only passed analyses are paid.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Incl. sampling and fees for the analyses.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The sampling points are to be documented. The water analyses are carried out</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">acc. to Drinking Water Ordinance, DIN EN 805 and the </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DVGW - worksheet W 291.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The test report is to be prepared in 3 - fold copies and handed over without being asked.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Prerequisites of the drinking water analysis:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">After the disinfection the water line is to be flushed through with drinking water,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">until the disinfectant is no longer detectable. Before that, the</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">sampling for the drinking water analysis must not be started.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note: The commissioning of the line takes place only when the analysis</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">               shows no coli - organisms and only after consultation with and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">               approval by the AG!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Microbiological drinking water analysis according to the Drinking Water Ordinance V, annex 1,2,5 (E-Coli, [PERSON_160], Aeromonas, colony count,  </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008291" RNoPart="0008">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Commissioning, functional test and acceptance</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The commissioning for the entire trade</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">is to be completely coordinated by the AN,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">commissioning and the functional tests are to be carried out in the presence of the AN, AG</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">taking into account the overall schedule.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The functional test has to take place before commissioning. The test is</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">to be recorded by the AN and the protocol submitted to the client or its</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">representative.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">It is to be assumed that the installations have to be put into operation in</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">stages. Costs for partial commissionings according to construction progress, unless</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">tendered separately, are to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">If repeated commissionings are necessary for reasons for which the building owner is not responsible, these costs will be passed on according to the causation</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">principle.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Commissioning, functional test and acceptance</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
          </BoQBody>
        </BoQCtgy>
        <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2008292" RNoPart="04">
          <LblTx>
            <p>
              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">CIVIL WORKS AND PIPES WATER LINE IN TRENCHLESS</span>
            </p>
            <p>
              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">CONSTRUCTION DIRECTIONAL BORES</span>
            </p>
          </LblTx>
          <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
          <BoQBody>
            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2008293" RNoPart="01">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Site setup directional bores</span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2008294">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note for the following items</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">site setup and traffic safety measures</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For these items the estimator has to observe the construction description, the special contract conditions and the execution design as the basis for the cost estimate.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The measure is carried out with 2 adjoining </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">directional bores 1 and 2.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The execution area of directional bore 1 includes the undercrossing of a forest track (skid trail, haul track for timber transport))</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution is in 1 overall section from station 0+580 to 0+745,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">L = approx. 165 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The execution area of directional bore 2 includes the undercrossing </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of a subsequent forest connecting track (gravel track) directly at the connection to directional bore 1 from station 0+745 to 0+990,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution is in 1 overall section, L = approx. 245 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The works located almost exclusively in the forest area.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Barriers and safeguarding of the construction activity are mainly needed for</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">safeguarding directly at the place of work.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The launch and reception pits are located in the aforementioned skid trails and forest connecting tracks.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">A common access route to both directional bores is located from [ADRESSE_018] to station 0+745 approx. 600 - 700 m, as well as from the edge of the village of Burg to station 0+745 approx. 1600 - 1700 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The forest tracks are mostly passable on a gravel layer and approx. 2,50 to 3,00 m wide. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The base item site setup is to be priced for the entire directional drilling works,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">that is for directional bores 1 and 2.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For the BE of the directional drilling rig itself, 2 separate items each are tendered.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note for the following items</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008295" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Setting up and clearing the site</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for directional drilling works PE DA = 355 mm</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The item includes setting up and clearing the site setup for all tendered directional drilling works (directional bore 1 and 2) </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Included are the necessary storage and working areas within the construction site area as well as their surfacing and removal. Areas used are to be restored to their former condition.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Payment is made according to the work performed.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Costs for keeping available on site, maintaining and operating the equipment, installations and facilities incl. rents, lease, fees and the like. are not paid with this lump sum, but in the following items with unit prices of the partial works concerned.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Setting up and clearing the site for directional drilling works PE DA = 355 mm</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008296" RNoPart="0002">
                    <Qty>2.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Setting up and clearing the site for directional drilling works PE DA = 355 mm</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The item includes setting up and clearing the complete directional drilling rig for the directional drilling works in the area of directional bores 1 and 2,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">billing in each case </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">1 piece per directional bore</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Furthermore the costs for keeping available on site, maintaining and operating the equipment, installations and facilities incl. rents, lease, fees.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note: The use of a directional drilling rig with a </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">               pulling force of at least 28 to is expressly required. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">               A rig with less pulling force is not permitted because of the </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">               boundary conditions!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">               The estimator has to take this into account expressly!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Setting up and clearing the site for directional drilling works PE DA = 355 mm</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008300" RNoPart="0003">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Prepare drilling fluid concept for the planned directional bores,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the required concept must contain the following points:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">1. </span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;">General information such as:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Location</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Bore</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Subsoil</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drilling equipment</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Solids control</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">2.</span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;"> Construction measure</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Description of the essential features of the measure</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Description of the functions and properties of the selected drilling suspension</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">3. </span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;">Drilling fluid programme with instructions for:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drilling fluid type</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drilling fluid recipe</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Density</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Rheology</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Filtration etc.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">  The drilling fluid programme must be matched to the project design and the geological         boundary provisions.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">4.</span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;"> Mixing water and drilling fluid demand</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Properties of the suspension to be used depending</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">  on the available mixing water</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Bore volume and pumping volume</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drilling fluid recipe</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Material demand and scope of supply</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">5. </span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;">Borehole hydraulics</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Characteristic data pilot bore </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Characteristic data reaming</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Characteristic data reaming pass</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Hydrostatic pressure</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">6. </span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;">Field tests to be carried out periodically</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">    The checking of the following parameters are to be taken into account here:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Time</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drilling progress</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Consumption</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drilling fluid recipe</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- ph - value, water hardness and salt content of the mixing water</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Acidity of the drilling suspension</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Apparent and plastic viscosity</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Yield point</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Gel strengths</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- API - water loss</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Filter cake thickness</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drilling fluid weight</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Sand content</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Drill cuttings inventory</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Organoleptic indicators such as colour and odour</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">7. </span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;">Solids control, reprocessing of the drilling fluid used</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">   Consideration of the individual necessary components such as e.g.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">-  Vibrating screens</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">-  Desilter</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">-  Centrifuge</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">8. </span>
                              <span style="text-decoration:underline;background:#FFFFFF;">Substance inputs into the environment</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">-  Current assessment by a qualified hygiene institute of the</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">   proposed drilling fluid system.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Prepare drilling fluid concept for the planned directional bores,</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2008301" RNoPart="02">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surveying </span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008302" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Surveying services - setting out</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution as horizontal setting out for the planned line route </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">and fixed points.</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The necessary digital drawing documents  are made available to the AN as DXF or DWG - file.</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Payment is made exclusively for points set out electro-optically (total station setting out or rover setting out).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Number of setting-out points for all 2 routes approx. 45 pieces.</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Points set out by hand are to be included in the overheads!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The execution in 2 sections is to be included in the price, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing here is lump sum for all 2 directional bores!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surveying services - setting out</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008303" RNoPart="0002">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surveying services - as-built</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Survey of all trades, lines constructed in position and height</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for checking and preparation of as-built drawings for</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the AG or the site management with total station or rover measurement.</span>
                              <br/>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Handover as digital CAD drawing (dwg - format 2007) and</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">in the form of list data (Ascii - format). As</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">coordinate system Gauß-Krüger, as height system</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DHHN12 is specified.</span>
                              <br/>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The list data must be unambiguously assignable to the</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">drawing objects and, besides number, code if applicable,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">easting, northing and Z coordinate (height), contain all</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">necessary information.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The surveys serve as the basis for laying,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">billing and as-built layout drawing.</span>
                              <br/>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Included are all necessary technical</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">facilities, materials, multiple trips to site, as well as</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the additional data collection at the responsible</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">surveying office (control points TP, HP etc.) and from</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">utility owners.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution takes place in parallel with the directional bore and preparation</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of the corresponding drilling log.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The drilling log is paid in the trade directional bore.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The measuring distances are, analogous to the drilling log, around approx. 5 - 6 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">if required (e.g. line correction etc.) the measuring distances can be reduced </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">down to 3 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The estimator has to take this into account and include it in the price here.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For both directional bore routes approx. 75 - 85 measuring points are to be reckoned with.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The execution in 2 sections is to be included in the price, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing here is lump sum for all 2 directional bores!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surveying services - as-built</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="GW_2008304" RNoPart="03">
              <LblTx>
                <p>
                  <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Civil works directional drilling works water line (main line) </span>
                </p>
              </LblTx>
              <NotApplBoQ>No</NotApplBoQ>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2019757">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Geotechnical note for the cost estimate of the items </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Horizontal directional drilling method </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Directional bore 1 forest track station 0+580 - 0+745,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Directional bore 2 forest track station 0+750 - 0+990.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The homogeneous zones are as follows:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB 5 B 3: moraine sand</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">HB 7 B 5: ground moraine, [PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Overview of all homogeneous zones in the area of trenchless construction.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Trenchless construction water line by the directional drilling method:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Listed here are all homogeneous zones in the area of trenchless construction from OK ground, but actually drilled through are only the HB 5 B 3 morain sand proportionally approx. 33 % and the HB 7 B 5 ground moraine proportionally approx. 67 %!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Please observe in the cost estimate!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 1, with 3 soil groups, soil group 1 GU DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 2 GU* DIN 18196 (gravel-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 3 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 1 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 15,000 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone A 1 fill,gravel soil class 3,4, according to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction measure of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions sand lower value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions sand upper value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions gravel lower value 50 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions gravel upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Moist density of soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 2000 to 2200 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Water content up to 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Relative density medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 5 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 2, with 2 soil groups, soil group 1 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), soil group 2 UM DIN 18196 (medium plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 1 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 2,000 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone A 2 fill, [PERSON_033] soil class 4, according to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction measure of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 55 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 75 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions sand lower value 10 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions sand upper value 30 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions gravel lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions gravel upper value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Moist density of soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 2000 to 2200 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Shear strength undrained from 20 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Shear strength undrained to 40 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Water content up to 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic from 0,5,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic to 0,75,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip from 4 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip to 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 5 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 3, with one soil group, soil group 1 HZ DIN 18196 (decomposed peat), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 1 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 2 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 1 peat soil class 2/4, according to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction measure of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 60 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 80 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions sand lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions sand upper value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions gravel lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fractions gravel upper value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Moist density of soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 over 1400 to 1600 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Shear strength undrained from 15 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Shear strength undrained to 30 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Water content over 20 to 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic from 0,5,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic to 0,75,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- Organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 10 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 4, with 2 soil groups, soil group 1 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), soil group 2 UM DIN 18196 (medium plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 3 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 40,000 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 2 weathered loam/slightly weathered ground moraine soil cl. 4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 55 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 75 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 10 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- bulk density of soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 above 1800 to 2000 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- undrained shear strength from 20 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- undrained shear strength to 60 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content above 10 to 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic from 0,5,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic to 0,75,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip from 4 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip to 25 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 greater than 3 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Execution</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 5,</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> with 3 soil groups, soil group 1 SW DIN 18196 (well-graded sand-gravel mixture), soil group 2 SU DIN 18196 (sand-[PERSON_033] mixture), soil group 3 SU* DIN 18196 (sand-[PERSON_033] mixture), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 0 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 4 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 13,000 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 3 moraine sand soil cl. 2,3,4, acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 1 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 3 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 2 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 30 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- bulk density of soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 above 1800 to 2000 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- undrained shear strength from 0,15 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- undrained shear strength to 0,5 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content above 20 to 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- relative density loose to medium dense,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 up to 3 %,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Execution</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zone 7</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, with 2 soil groups, soil group 1 UL DIN 18196 (slightly plastic [PERSON_033]), soil group 2 UM DIN 18196 (medium plastic [PERSON_033]), depth of upper horizon of the homogeneous zone from 1 m, depth of lower horizon of the homogeneous zone to 6 m,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">estimated share of the homogeneous zone in the total excavation quantity 28 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">local designation homogeneous zone B 5  ground moraine soil cl. 4,(6) depending on share and size of the cobbles and bboulders/with firm consistency soil cl. 6 acc. to DIN 18300 (2012-09).</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construction project of geotechnical category 2 DIN 4020, grain size distribution range DIN EN ISO 17892-4:</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_108] upper value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] lower value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- [PERSON_033] upper value 70 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand lower value 20 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions sand upper value 40 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel lower value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fractions gravel upper value 15 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) lower value 0 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction cobbles DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Co) upper value 5 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction boulders DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (Bo) upper value 3 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- mass fraction large boulders DIN EN ISO 14688-1 (LBo) upper value 1 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- bulk density of soil DIN EN ISO 17892-2 or DIN 18125-2 above 2000 to 2200 kg/m3,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- undrained shear strength from 60 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- undrained shear strength to 150 kPa,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- water content above 5 to 10 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic from 0,75,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- consistency index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ic to 1,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip from 12 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plasticity index DIN EN ISO 17892-12 Ip to 30 %,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- organic mass fraction DIN 18128 up to 3 %.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Geotechnical note on pricing the items </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2030726">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Note on pricing the launch and reception pits:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For the two directional bores 1 and 2, one launch and [PERSON_034] each</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">are tendered.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The directional bores are each planned in 1 piece.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Should, contrary to expectations, an additional pit for which the AN himself is responsible become necessary between the launch and reception pits during the directional drilling works in order to carry them out, it is to be included in the price of the overall directional bore and is not paid separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Should an additional pit become necessary for reasons for which the AN is not responsible (e.g. geological peculiarities such as very large boulders or heavy root systems),</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">these are paid in surcharge items to the launch and reception pits.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">In any case, the matter must be clarified jointly between AG and AN before execution! </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For the case of a failed bore during the pilot bore, separate surcharge</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">items are tendered and are also paid there.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Note on pricing the launch and reception pits:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008306" RNoPart="0001">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">[PERSON_073]</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for pipe DA 355</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construct and remove open excavation pit as [PERSON_073] for the horizontal bore, incl. keeping available on site the additional parts required for the bore,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for pipe DA 355</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Dimensions acc. to [PERSON_125] AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Depth from GOK, pipeline depths see longitudinal section,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">restoration of the ground surface is paid </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Shoring, shoring penetration acc. to [PERSON_125] of the AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">To be included in the price: </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">install shoring according to structural requirements, keep available on site and remove, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">excavate, backfill and compact excavation pit base acc. to the ZTV and guidelines for excavations in traffic areas (ZTVA-StB), </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">load soil, transport within the site, store and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">re-install, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">No shoring parts may remain in the soil.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Dewatering open/ closed acc. to [PERSON_125] of the contractor with the aim of keeping the excavation pit base free of water, design water level for temporary works according to expert report see below.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing here is per piece for directional bore 1 forest track </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">station approx. 0+580 - 0+745.Length approx. 165 m!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The [PERSON_073] lies between RKS 4 and RKS 5</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 4 (directional bore ends approx. 10-12 m before RKS 4/25):</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,00 - 0,40 m topsoil, [PERSON_033]                                                                          0,40 - 1,90 m HB B 2 weathered loam, [PERSON_033], slightly weathered                                                                 ground moraine</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                    1,90 - 2,80 m HB B 4 moraine gravel (</span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">at approx. 2,24 m groundwater                                                            encountered)        </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                    2,80 - 4,00 m HB B 5 ground moraine,[PERSON_033] </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 5:       0,00 - 0,50 m  HB A 1 fill fine- coarse gravel                  </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,50 - 1,70 m  HB B 2 weathered loam, [PERSON_033], slightly weathered                                                                 ground moraine</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   1,70 - 4,00 m  HB B 5  ground moraine,[PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                                                       </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">(no [PERSON_029] encountered down to 4,0 m)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 6:       0,00 - 0,40 m   HB A 1 fill fine- coarse gravel </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,40  1,50 m    HB B 2 [PERSON_033], slightly weathered  ground moraine </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   1,50 - 3,00 m   HB B 5 ground moraine, [PERSON_033]. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                                                        </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">(no [PERSON_029] encountered down to 3,0 m)</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">[PERSON_073] for pipe DA 355</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
