                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2030725" RNoPart="0005">
                    <Qty>2.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the items launch and reception pits</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for necessary intermediate pits for which the AN is not responsible.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">[PERSON_175]</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for pipe DA 355</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Construct and remove open excavation pit as [PERSON_175] for the horizontal bore, incl. keeping available on site the additional parts required for the bore,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for pipe DA 355</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Dimensions acc. to [PERSON_125] AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Depth from GOK, pipeline depths see longitudinal section,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">restoration of the ground surface is paid </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Shoring, shoring penetration acc. to [PERSON_125] of the AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">To be included in the price: </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">install shoring according to structural requirements, keep available on site and remove, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">excavate, backfill and compact excavation pit base acc. to the ZTV and guidelines for excavations in traffic areas (ZTVA-StB), </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">load soil, transport within the site, store and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">re-install, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">No shoring parts may remain in the soil.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Dewatering open/ closed acc. to [PERSON_125] of the contractor with the aim of keeping the excavation pit base free of water, design water level for temporary works according to expert report see below.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing here are expressly only as necessary and after prior consultation with the AG, per piece!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the items launch and reception pits for necessary intermediate pits for which the AN is not responsible.</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008309" RNoPart="0006">
                    <Qty>10.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the [ORT_030] soil for [PERSON_121]</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">including hand excavation,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">excavate, for exposing lines, from ground surface, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">store excavated material at the side, backfill and compact,</span>
                              <br/>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">excavation depth up to 4,0 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">base width in m as required,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">in the area of lines with unknown, o.r. inexact position.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing according to on-site measurement.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the [ORT_030] soil for [PERSON_121], </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008310" RNoPart="0007">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge for additional effort coordination operators of utility lines </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">of any kind</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge as payment for coordination with operators of utility and supply lines of any kind. Checking in places that the bore is free of damage, as well as determining the depth position, are to be included in the price. Search trenches are paid separately.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution is to be included in the price for 2 consecutive directional bores.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is once as a lump sum for both directional bores!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge for additional effort coordination operators of utility lines </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008311" RNoPart="0008">
                    <Qty>165.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Pilot bore 1</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> Pipes PE DA 355.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Driving the pilot bore on the planned bore axis according to layout and elevation drawings,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">including the ancillary services necessary for this from entry to exit of the drill head from the ground with Walk-Over- / Wire-Line .</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is by pull-in length, additional effort for earlier piercing of the drill head into the ground in order to reach the level with the pilot bore is to be included in the price. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The provision, keeping available on site and operation of a drilling fluid- recycling plant is likewise to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing for the undercrossing of the forest track and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">1 ditch culvert pipe DN 500.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution is in 1 overall section.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Cover from OK ground approx. 1,70 - 2,60,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">see longitudinal section approx. station 0+580 - 0+745. Length approx. 165 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The geology present is described in detail in the item directional bore 1</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing for the undercrossing of the forest track and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">1 ditch culvert pipe DN 500. </span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pilot bore 1 pipes PE DA 355.</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008312" RNoPart="0009">
                    <Qty>85.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to pilot bore 1 for failed bore PE DA 355, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the item pilot bore for failed bores, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">includes all Necessary expenses for equipment, material and personnel for pulling back and restarting or bypassing obstacles.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing for the undercrossing of the forest track and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">1 ditch culvert pipe DN 500.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to pilot bore 1 for failed bore PE DA 355, </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008313" RNoPart="0010">
                    <Qty>165.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Horizontal</span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;"> directional bore 1</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for PE100RC TW AD/WD 355/32,2 mm </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">PAS 1075 [PERSON_129] 3</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Reaming of the borehole to the required final diameter diameter including all ancillary services necessary for this with jetting support as well as addition of bentonite suspension to support the borehole wall matched to the subsoil according to the ground investigation, a certificate of non-objection is to be submitted.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The provision, keeping available on site and operation of a drilling fluid- </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">recycling plant is to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The ballasting of the line with [PERSON_029] against pipe buoyancy for the pipe pull-in is likewise to be included in the price!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">With logging related to drilling progress acc. to DVGW GW 321, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">all necessary measurements incl. laying log,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">pull-in of the continuous pipeline by retrieving the drill rods in the driven cavity for PE100RC TW AD/WD 355/32,2 mm PAS 1075 [PERSON_129] 3, (pipe material is paid separately,see item in the trade pipelines </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for directional bores).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Incl. roller track acc. to [PERSON_125] of the AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pulling force limitation according to manufacturer's specifications for the pipe material,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the drilling fluid must not be disposed of in the terrain (forest) and must not get into the water ditch, or onto the ditch embankment etc., </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">To be included in the price is the sampling of the drilling mud acc. to LAGA, as well as the proper recycling/disposal according to waste code number 010504 of the muds and wastes from freshwater drilling,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The recycling/disposal is to be proven, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For contaminated drilling muds supplements are paid,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and cover acc. to pIan template‚</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">incl. retained sample of the drilling suspension before and after the works.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Cover from OK ground directional bore approx. 1,70 - 2,60.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pipe outside diameter OD 355 mm,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the PE pipes are to be kept clean, all contamination of the pipe (for example betonite ingress) is to be avoided, any cleaning of the pipe that may be necessary (flushing, etc.) is at the expense of the AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is for the bored length in the ground including launch and reception pits corresponding to the length of the installed pipeline,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">expenses for the entry / exit section between entry at the ground surface up to the launch / [PERSON_034] are to be included in the price,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">billing areas are specified in the longitudinal section.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution is in 1 overall section in the area of the undercrossing of the</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">forest track station approx. 0+580 - 0+745. Length approx. 165 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">According to the ram core soundings 4/25, 5/25 and 6/25 the geology is as follows:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zones acc. to DIN 18300,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 4 (directional bore ends approx. 10-12 m before RKS 4/25):</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,00 - 0,40 m topsoil, [PERSON_033]                                                                          0,40 - 1,90 m HB B 2 weathered loam, [PERSON_033], slightly weathered                                                                 ground moraine</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                    1,90 - 2,80 m HB B 4 moraine gravel</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                    2,80 - 4,00 m HB B 5 ground moraine,[PERSON_033] </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 5:       0,00 - 0,50 m  HB A 1 fill fine- coarse gravel                  </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,50 - 1,70 m  HB B 2 weathered loam, [PERSON_033], slightly weathered                                                                 ground moraine</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   1,70 - 4,00 m  HB B 5  ground moraine,[PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 6:       0,00 - 0,40 m   HB A 1 fill fine- coarse gravel </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,40  1,50 m    HB B 2 [PERSON_033], slightly weathered  ground moraine </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   1,50 - 3,00 m   HB B 5 ground moraine, [PERSON_033].</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Horizontal directional bore 1 for PE100RC TW AD/WD 355/32,2 mm </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008314" RNoPart="0011">
                    <Qty>240.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Pilot bore 2</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> Pipes PE DA 355.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Driving the pilot bore on the planned bore axis according to layout and elevation drawings,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">including the ancillary services necessary for this from entry to exit of the drill head from the ground with Walk-Over- / Wire-Line .</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is by pull-in length, additional effort for earlier piercing of the drill head into the ground in order to reach the level with the pilot bore is to be included in the price. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The provision, keeping available on site and operation of a drilling fluid- recycling plant is likewise to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing for the undercrossing of forest track</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">and 2 ditch culvert pipes DN 300,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">station approx. 0+750 - 0+990.L = approx. 240 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Cover from OK ground approx. 1,70 - 2,60 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">see longitudinal section station 0+750 - 0+990.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution is in 1 overall section.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The geology present is described in detail in the item directional bore 2</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pilot bore 2 pipes PE DA 355.</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008315" RNoPart="0012">
                    <Qty>120.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to pilot bore 2 for failed bore PE DA 355, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to the item pilot bore for failed bores, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">includes all Necessary expenses for equipment, material and personnel for pulling back and restarting or bypassing obstacles.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing for execution and billing for the </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">undercrossing of forest track and 2 ditch culvert pipes DN 300,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">station 0+750 - 0+990.L = approx. 240 m.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge to pilot bore 2 for failed bore PE DA 355, </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008316" RNoPart="0013">
                    <Qty>240.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Horizontal </span>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">directional bore 2</span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> for PE100RC TW AD/WD 355/32,2 mm </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">PAS 1075 [PERSON_129] 3</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">and a bi - axially oriented polymer - matrix - film with embedded metallic diffussion barrier as permeation barrier and a protective jacket of </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">modified polyolefin compound. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Incl. additional effort in the area of the welded joints.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Reaming of the borehole to the required final diameter diameter including all ancillary services necessary for this with jetting support as well as addition of bentonite suspension to support the borehole wall matched to the subsoil according to the ground investigation, a certificate of non-objection is to be submitted.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The provision, keeping available on site and operation of a drilling fluid- </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">recycling plant is to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The ballasting of the line with [PERSON_029] against pipe buoyancy for the pipe pull-in is likewise to be included in the price!</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">With logging related to drilling progress acc. to DVGW GW 321, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">all necessary measurements incl. laying log,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">pull-in of the continuous pipeline by retrieving the drill rods in the driven cavity for PE100RC TW AD/WD 355/32,2 mm PAS 1075 [PERSON_129] 3, (pipe material is paid separately,see item in the trade pipelines </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">for directional bores).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Incl. roller track acc. to [PERSON_125] of the AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;"> </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pulling force limitation according to manufacturer's specifications for the pipe material,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the drilling fluid must not be disposed of in the terrain and must not get into drainage ditches, or onto the ditch embankment etc., </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">To be included in the price is the sampling of the drilling mud acc. to LAGA, as well as the proper recycling/disposal according to waste code number 010504 of the muds and wastes from freshwater drilling,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The recycling/disposal is to be proven, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For contaminated drilling muds supplements are paid,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and cover acc. to pIan template‚</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">incl. retained sample of the drilling suspension before and after the works.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Cover from OK ground approx. 1,70 - 2,60 m,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">see longitudinal section station 0+750 - 0+990, L = approx. 240 m.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Pipe outside diameter OD 355 mm,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the PE pipes are to be kept clean, all contamination of the pipe (for example betonite ingress) is to be avoided, any cleaning of the pipe that may be necessary (flushing, etc.) is at the expense of the AN.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing is for the bored length in the ground including launch and reception pits corresponding to the length of the installed pipeline,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">expenses for the entry / exit section between entry at the ground surface up to the launch / [PERSON_034] are to be included in the price,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">billing areas are specified in the longitudinal section.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution and billing for the undercrossing of forest track and </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">2 ditch culvert pipes DN 300, station 0+750 - 0+990.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution is in 1 overall section.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">According to the ram core soundings the geology is as follows:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Homogeneous zones acc. to DIN 18300,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;"/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 6:       0,00 - 0,40 m   HB A 1 fill fine- coarse gravel </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,40  1,50 m    HB B 2 [PERSON_033], slightly weathered  ground moraine </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   1,50 - 3,00 m   HB B 5 ground moraine, [PERSON_033].                   </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 7:       0,00 - 0,40 m   HB A 1 fill fine- coarse gravel </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,40  1,60 m    HB B 2 [PERSON_033], slightly weathered  ground moraine </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   1,60 - 2,00 m   HB B 5 ground moraine, [PERSON_033]. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 8:       0,00 - 0,50 m   HB A 1 fill fine- coarse gravel </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,50  0,90 m    HB A 2 fill [PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   0,90 - 1,40 m   HB B 1 peat</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                   1,40 - 4,00 m   HB B 3 moraine sand, fine sand.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 9:        0,00 - 0,40 m   HB A 1  fill fine- coarse gravel </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                    0,40 - 1,60 m  HB B 2  weathered loam, [PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                    1,60 - 4,00 m  HB B 3  moraine sand, fine to medium sand.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">RKS 10:       0,00 - 0,10 m  forest soil, [PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                     0,10 - 1,20 m  HB B 2  weathered loam, [PERSON_033]</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">                     1,20 - 4,00 m  HB B 3  moraine sand, fine sand.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Horizontal directional bore 2 for PE100RC TW AD/WD 355/32,2 mm </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008320" RNoPart="0014">
                    <Qty>8.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Difficulty surcharge to the item directional bore 1 and 2 </span>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">PE DA 355 for:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Blowout risk in areas with a relatively small cover </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">(geological necessity) of approx. 1,60 m to 2,50 m from OK line </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">to OK ground.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Both directional bores is located in the forest track area.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">  </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The following services are to be included in the price:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Immediately on detecting a blowout, pump off, pick up and properly dispose of escaped suspension (drilling mud).</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">To be included in the price is the sampling of the drilling mud acc. to LAGA, as well as the proper recycling/disposal according to waste code number 010504 of the muds and wastes from freshwater drilling,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The recycling/disposal is to be proven, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">For contaminated drilling muds supplements are paid.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The disposal of the drilling mud of the directional bore is paid in the </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">item directional bore.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Clean the area of the forest track surface at the point of escape.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing only where a blowout is actually detected, by piece per </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">point of escape.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Difficulty surcharge to the item directional bore 1 and 2 PE DA 355 for:</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008321" RNoPart="0015">
                    <Qty>405.000</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge horizontal directional bore PE DA 355 for drilling logs pulling force </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">as surcharge to the horizontal directional bores 1 and 2 for PE100RC TW AD/WD 355/ 32,2 mm PAS 1075 [PERSON_129] 3,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">by means of pulling force measurement between pipeline and pull rods as proof of compliance with the maximum pulling force on the pipe material,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution in 2 spatially separate sections is to be included in the price, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">the sections / logs to be designated accordingly for unambiguous assignment. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing here is in lfm for both directional bores!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge horizontal directional bore PE DA 355 for drilling logs pulling force </span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008322" RNoPart="0016">
                    <Qty>20.000</Qty>
                    <QU>t</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Surcharge horizontal directional bore PE DA 355 for </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">disposal of drilling mud acc. to EBV [KENNZEICHEN_001]* (VwV Z1.1)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Supplement to the directional drilling method for the proper disposal of drilling mud,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">waste code number 010504.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">acc. to classification value EBV [KENNZEICHEN_001]* (VwV Z1.1)</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Execution in 2 spatially separate sections is to be included in the price.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Billing here is in tonnes for both directional bores,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="text-align:justify;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">in each case only the surcharge item applicable according to the analysis is billed!</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
