                          <ChVIdent>10</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                      </STLBBau>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">End plug of PE, with welding ends, for pressure pipeline of PE, joined by electrofusion welding, for drinking water DIN EN 12201, DVGW GW 335-B2, DN/OD 355, SDR 11.</span>
                            </p>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p>
                                <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">End plug PE electrofusion welding DN/OD355 SDR11</span>
                              </p>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="GW_2008603">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Notes on the following item special flange:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">General preliminary remark</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The fittings to be offered must be supplied as a set of welding stub and a backing flange matched to the dimension. The welding stubs must be made of material according to the PE100+ Association and must comply with DIN EN 12201 and DIN EN 1555 with regard to dimensions, tolerances and quality requirements. The backing flanges must be made of [PERSON_089] with plastic coating acc. to DIN EN 10310. Proof of manufacture on the basis of a quality assurance system acc. to DIN EN ISO 9001 is to be provided. For all fittings a certificate acc. to DIN EN 10204 from the manufacturer is to be submitted. The PE fitting body must be made by injection moulding, alternatively from one piece of homogeneous semi-finished product. Semi-finished products made from wound rod or other subsequently applied reinforcements are not permitted.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The stub must be drilled through according to the hole pattern acc. to DIN EN 1092-1 PN 10 or PN 16. The bolt holes thereby lie closer to the pipe outside diameter. The backing flange must have the same drilling pattern. This allows the transition of equal nominal diameter to, for example, valves or steel flanges. </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The stub must be designed to suit plastics in order to be able to receive the correspondingly shaped backing flange, in order to counteract deformation. This brings about full pressure load capacity of the flange joint corresponding to the pipe dimensioning.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The stub is to be provided with an EPDM O-ring seal corresponding to the dimension.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">The spigot ends are to be executed in long form in order to be able to carry out both an HE butt welding and an HW welding.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="font-weight:bold;background:#FFFFFF;">Standards/guidelines/approvals/certificates</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DIN EN 12201, DIN EN 1092-1, DVS 2207, DVS 2210, DIN EN 10204, DIN EN ISO 9001, DIN EN ISO 50001, DVGW W 400-2, DVGW GW 335 DVGW: DV-8606BT0423 and DV-8611BT0424</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Inspection certificate 3.1 acc. to DIN EN ISO 10204 on the semi-finished product of the processed raw material stating MFR and OIT; only PE100 material acc. to PE100+ Association</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Manufacturer certified acc. to ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 50001:2011</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                          </Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt>
                              <p/>
                            </TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="GW_2008604" RNoPart="0007">
                    <Qty>1.000</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">PE100 special flange, PN 16 drilled</span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">PE100 special flange with backing flange of [PERSON_089] with plastic coating acc. to DIN EN 10310 for connection to valves of the same nominal diameter, with EPDM O-ring, designed for full pressure rating, drilled acc. to DIN EN 1092-1, PN 16, with long weld-on end for HW welding, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p style="margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;">
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">supply and execution for restrained transition PE - pipe DA 355 to flange for ductile cast iron pipe DN 300.</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- including EPDM O - ring</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- plastic-coated steel flange</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">- long welding end, suitable for E - socket - welding</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">DN: 300</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">d1: 355</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">SDR: 11</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">PN: 16</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">[PERSON_129]/manufacturer:</span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">special flange, PN 16 drilled,</span>
                            </p>
                            <p/>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">[FIRMA_112] GmbH, </span>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                              <span style="background:#FFFFFF;">Ernst - Heinkel - Straße 2</span>
                            </p>
